WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:32.450
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:32.720 --> 00:33.930
He's here.

3
00:57.745 --> 00:58.872
Who are you?

4
01:02.125 --> 01:03.626
It's been a while…

5
01:06.087 --> 01:06.921
Emi.

6
01:08.047 --> 01:08.923
No.

7
01:09.674 --> 01:10.967
Minamoto Shunsuke.

8
01:11.467 --> 01:12.760
Mister

9
01:13.386 --> 01:14.429
Ito?

10
01:21.436 --> 01:22.896
Get some good rest.

11
02:29.963 --> 02:31.756
THE BLUE ROAD

12
02:34.259 --> 02:38.680
FUNERAL HOME

13
02:39.389 --> 02:41.057
It finally makes sense.

14
02:42.767 --> 02:46.145
Your uncle was killed in the serial murders of '87…

15
02:48.147 --> 02:50.191
and Emi reenacted those murders.

16
02:50.692 --> 02:53.152
That's why you were so fixated on him.

17
02:54.279 --> 02:58.324
From the beginning, his victims never mattered to you.

18
02:58.408 --> 03:04.789
You were just using the current case to catch the original from back then.

19
03:05.540 --> 03:07.709
Tell me I'm wrong!

20
03:13.089 --> 03:15.466
And you call yourself a detective?

21
03:19.262 --> 03:21.306
Well, aren't you a fucking prick.

22
03:24.726 --> 03:25.935
Speak so I can understand.

23
03:26.019 --> 03:28.563
If you're in Korea, learn to speak Korean properly.

24
03:30.648 --> 03:31.482
Hey.

25
03:33.026 --> 03:36.821
Who was it that got so affected by Lee Hyeon-seo's death that they saw red,

26
03:37.447 --> 03:39.657
acting like some feral beast?

27
03:41.826 --> 03:44.287
And then you froze up like some idiot.

28
03:46.122 --> 03:47.832
I said, I can't understand you.

29
03:48.666 --> 03:50.460
And you call yourself a detective?

30
04:00.595 --> 04:02.263
Screw you!

31
04:16.611 --> 04:17.445
Are you okay?

32
04:26.913 --> 04:27.955
That was a cheap shot!

33
04:29.624 --> 04:30.792
You son of a bitch!

34
04:43.930 --> 04:45.848
That hurt, you bastard!

35
04:48.142 --> 04:49.644
Fuck you!

36
05:00.238 --> 05:02.281
Kim Seok!

37
05:02.365 --> 05:03.991
Listen!

38
05:06.619 --> 05:08.246
I understand about your uncle.

39
05:11.124 --> 05:12.667
But the bottom line is,

40
05:13.626 --> 05:16.838
the case from the past and Emi's case

41
05:17.338 --> 05:19.006
are two separate things.

42
05:20.716 --> 05:21.759
You need to face it.

43
05:25.471 --> 05:27.181
That's the only way to catch

44
05:27.682 --> 05:29.100
your uncle's killer.

45
05:57.003 --> 05:59.338
Perhaps it was something I inherited from my mother…

46
06:02.049 --> 06:05.052
but I, too, could hear and see strange things since a young age.

47
06:07.847 --> 06:09.474
I still do, from time to time.

48
06:11.267 --> 06:14.479
It was hardly a gift of any sort.

49
06:15.146 --> 06:16.272
More like a curse.

50
06:18.107 --> 06:22.153
My mother performed a suppression rite to try and prevent my shamanic calling.

51
06:23.196 --> 06:24.238
It was painful,

52
06:25.656 --> 06:29.202
but I got through it thanks to Uncle Du-yeong, who helped my mom.

53
06:56.521 --> 06:59.023
Seok! Don't succumb to it.

54
06:59.106 --> 07:03.694
Look at me. Don't close your eyes. Don't succumb to it.

55
07:03.778 --> 07:05.613
Seok. Look at me.

56
07:05.696 --> 07:07.114
Don't be afraid.

57
07:09.450 --> 07:11.911
Don't be afraid, okay?

58
07:13.454 --> 07:14.789
Don't succumb to it.

59
07:15.957 --> 07:16.832
Seok.

60
07:17.750 --> 07:18.793
Kim Seok!

61
07:18.876 --> 07:22.296
If it weren't for Uncle Du-yeong, I wouldn't have gotten through it.

62
07:25.466 --> 07:27.093
That man was like a father to me.

63
07:27.176 --> 07:28.636
DO NOT ENTER INVESTIGATION IN PROGRESS

64
07:32.306 --> 07:34.141
But before I even became an adult…

65
07:43.150 --> 07:44.944
the uncle who was like a father to me…

66
08:10.928 --> 08:13.014
In the end, the culprit was never caught.

67
08:17.518 --> 08:20.104
Police investigations were a joke back then.

68
08:22.148 --> 08:25.776
So you became a cop, and history repeated itself.

69
08:26.986 --> 08:28.654
Like fate.

70
08:31.824 --> 08:34.952
I'm alive thanks to Uncle Du-yeong.

71
08:42.209 --> 08:43.711
It's strange, isn't it?

72
08:45.796 --> 08:47.214
We weren't even blood.

73
08:54.096 --> 08:54.930
My daughter…

74
09:00.019 --> 09:01.437
likes Korea.

75
09:03.522 --> 09:04.815
BoA.

76
09:06.067 --> 09:09.445
She really likes Korean music.

77
09:12.198 --> 09:15.660
That's why I studied Korean.

78
09:17.995 --> 09:22.500
So that I could talk to Rumi more often.

79
09:24.335 --> 09:25.336
But

80
09:26.462 --> 09:28.589
she's not my real daughter.

81
09:33.511 --> 09:35.805
She's the ex-husband's kid.

82
09:39.767 --> 09:41.977
But I cherish her more.

83
09:43.646 --> 09:44.689
That's why

84
09:45.356 --> 09:47.441
it doesn't matter whether you're blood or not.

85
09:48.025 --> 09:49.860
That has nothing to do with love.

86
10:01.580 --> 10:02.415
I'm sorry.

87
10:02.915 --> 10:03.749
No.

88
10:04.500 --> 10:08.087
Thanks to you, we solved the case, and I might even get a promotion.

89
10:08.754 --> 10:11.215
And if I can just keep up with child support,

90
10:12.842 --> 10:15.177
I'll be able to see Rumi more often.

91
10:15.678 --> 10:17.179
That's good to hear.

92
10:17.263 --> 10:18.389
Yeah.

93
10:26.105 --> 10:27.064
Cheers.

94
10:41.996 --> 10:42.955
Inose.

95
10:44.039 --> 10:44.874
Yeah?

96
10:45.750 --> 10:46.876
I have

97
10:48.753 --> 10:49.837
something to show you.

98
11:07.938 --> 11:09.774
You put all of this together?

99
11:12.485 --> 11:13.527
If you see here…

100
11:15.362 --> 11:17.239
The 1987 serial murders in Korea…

101
11:17.323 --> 11:18.866
FIRST SUSPECTED MURDER JANUARY 1987

102
11:18.949 --> 11:20.451
SECOND SUSPECTED MURDER MARCH 1987

103
11:20.534 --> 11:21.786
…tallied at four.

104
11:21.869 --> 11:23.746
THIRD SUSPECTED MURDER DECEMBER 1987

105
11:23.829 --> 11:25.748
The last victim was Hong Du-yeong.

106
11:25.831 --> 11:27.374
FOURTH SUSPECTED MURDER HONG DU-YEONG

107
11:31.587 --> 11:34.340
Emi twisted his victims' limbs while they were still alive.

108
11:34.840 --> 11:35.674
But

109
11:37.176 --> 11:40.805
the victims from '87 didn't show signs of hemorrhaging in their pupils.

110
11:41.806 --> 11:42.681
In other words,

111
11:43.849 --> 11:44.975
the original

112
11:45.893 --> 11:48.479
twisted the limbs

113
11:49.063 --> 11:50.231
of the dead.

114
11:52.066 --> 11:53.734
-Let's make an assumption. -Okay.

115
11:54.860 --> 11:58.656
Let's say Emi learned about the original killer's method of '87,

116
11:58.739 --> 12:01.867
copied, and improved on it for his own pleasure.

117
12:03.661 --> 12:07.081
There's one guy who would know about that method, right?

118
12:09.750 --> 12:11.418
The original?

119
12:13.587 --> 12:14.964
The original…

120
12:18.175 --> 12:21.929
I suppose that photographer might know something about it.

121
12:23.264 --> 12:26.934
I'll go back to Japan and pay Mikogami a visit.

122
12:29.395 --> 12:30.396
Let's give it our all.

123
12:35.818 --> 12:37.486
DIGGING INTO THE RUMORS! THE TRUTH FILES

124
12:38.070 --> 12:41.407
Today's story is from our neighboring country, Korea,

125
12:42.157 --> 12:45.661
about a grotesque serial killer, who operated across both Japan and Korea

126
12:45.744 --> 12:49.415
and died during the course of his arrest.

127
12:49.498 --> 12:55.045
Rumor has it that this case is related to the fourth-largest conglomerate in Japan,

128
12:55.129 --> 12:58.048
Minamoto Pharmaceuticals, no less!

129
12:59.383 --> 13:00.634
What?

130
13:01.135 --> 13:06.473
Currently, police in both countries are keeping the case under wraps

131
13:06.557 --> 13:09.393
due to the ongoing Japan-Korea World Cup.

132
13:09.476 --> 13:12.313
But rumor has it that the killer Emi Shunsuke was actually

133
13:12.396 --> 13:14.565
a love child of Minamoto Pharmaceuticals!

134
13:15.190 --> 13:18.903
He was none other than Minamoto Shunsuke,

135
13:18.986 --> 13:21.655
an illegitimate child!

136
13:21.739 --> 13:25.159
It looks like their intel is faster and more detailed than us.

137
13:25.242 --> 13:28.454
On top of that, a lot of people watch this show.

138
13:28.537 --> 13:32.750
There's also a rumor that Minamoto Pharmaceuticals is connected to Korea.

139
13:34.001 --> 13:37.713
Apparently, Emi Shinsuke's mother is Korean.

140
13:37.796 --> 13:40.341
I heard she was a number one requested hostess.

141
13:41.425 --> 13:44.511
There's even been an anonymous tip from the Minamoto family.

142
13:45.012 --> 13:48.140
About Emi killing his pet dog when he was a kid.

143
13:48.223 --> 13:50.726
If that's actually true, it's terrifying.

144
13:58.442 --> 13:59.318
Hey!

145
13:59.944 --> 14:01.195
You there, slacker!

146
14:06.575 --> 14:08.827
Watching TV during work hours?

147
14:09.411 --> 14:10.871
Apologies, sir.

148
14:11.705 --> 14:13.082
The case is over, and yet…

149
14:14.041 --> 14:15.918
Where's Inose? When's he coming back?

150
14:16.669 --> 14:17.670
No idea, sir.

151
14:18.837 --> 14:21.715
I did hear that he booked his plane ticket.

152
14:23.175 --> 14:25.970
What the hell is he thinking?

153
14:29.139 --> 14:30.307
Chief Shimizu.

154
14:32.101 --> 14:34.937
The case is closed, right?

155
14:38.607 --> 14:41.819
From here on out, the higher-ups will handle it.

156
14:41.902 --> 14:42.736
By higher-ups,

157
14:43.570 --> 14:44.989
do you mean Public Security?

158
14:46.407 --> 14:49.076
We can't let this become a political issue with Korea.

159
14:50.786 --> 14:53.539
I'm saying it's no longer our responsibility.

160
15:07.219 --> 15:11.265
PRIME HOTEL, ROOM 1206 LI YOON-OK

161
15:32.911 --> 15:34.496
What, is Korea your playground?

162
15:36.331 --> 15:37.166
Well?

163
15:38.167 --> 15:39.877
You disrespectful bastards.

164
16:09.990 --> 16:11.700
Inspector Kim Seok is here.

165
16:12.743 --> 16:14.036
Mu-seong, go wait outside.

166
16:18.540 --> 16:19.500
But

167
16:20.667 --> 16:22.002
Mr. Seo said I should be--

168
16:22.086 --> 16:24.546
You should know that my will is Mr. Seo's will.

169
16:37.309 --> 16:39.728
Congratulations on arresting Shunsuke.

170
16:39.812 --> 16:42.231
Though he did end up dead.

171
16:43.065 --> 16:48.112
Mr. Seo also asked me to convey his appreciation for all your hard work.

172
16:48.195 --> 16:50.197
Enough of that. What do you want?

173
17:01.792 --> 17:06.547
You don't think this case is over yet, do you?

174
17:07.923 --> 17:12.594
You think there's another culprit besides the dead Shunsuke.

175
17:13.512 --> 17:15.430
In any case, Shunsuke is dead,

176
17:16.431 --> 17:19.810
and because of the World Cup, the public has no interest in this case.

177
17:20.811 --> 17:22.646
Why don't you just get to the point?

178
17:25.524 --> 17:27.401
You're threatening me to stop investigating.

179
17:27.484 --> 17:30.195
What's this? Minamoto? A contract?

180
17:30.696 --> 17:33.991
You pathetic gangsters sure try, don't you?

181
17:35.492 --> 17:36.618
So,

182
17:38.078 --> 17:39.538
isn't this a threat?

183
17:46.503 --> 17:48.714
What does that bastard Seo Hyun-tae want?

184
17:51.425 --> 17:53.010
Are you ready for this?

185
17:53.093 --> 17:54.011
What?

186
17:57.598 --> 17:58.724
Will you

187
18:00.434 --> 18:02.436
stake your life on this investigation?

188
18:05.689 --> 18:09.026
Go and tell Seo Hyun-tae, who you call "Mr. Seo,"

189
18:09.109 --> 18:10.611
to cut the bullshit.

190
18:12.654 --> 18:13.822
Tell him to stop hiding

191
18:13.906 --> 18:16.200
so I can see his damn mug and ask what his deal is.

192
18:16.700 --> 18:17.993
You know Korean, right?

193
18:20.996 --> 18:22.873
Absolutely ridiculous.

194
18:35.969 --> 18:36.803
Inose.

195
18:38.263 --> 18:40.933
Seo Hyun-tae's guys are in Seoul right now.

196
18:41.433 --> 18:42.684
Please look into it.

197
18:49.107 --> 18:50.275
Hello, Professor.

198
18:50.359 --> 18:53.570
I'm Kim Seok from the Seoul Police. We met the other day.

199
18:54.363 --> 18:55.197
Yes.

200
18:56.490 --> 18:58.492
You mean the place we met last time, right?

201
18:58.575 --> 18:59.826
It's that bastard, right?

202
19:03.163 --> 19:05.415
He's just straight-up bossing me around.

203
19:06.833 --> 19:09.628
Who does he think he is, my boss?

204
19:14.591 --> 19:16.385
I want to go home already.

205
19:23.016 --> 19:24.518
I did agree to give it my all.

206
19:25.185 --> 19:27.312
Ito's men are in Seoul?

207
19:27.396 --> 19:31.149
Ito…

208
19:42.619 --> 19:44.746
What on earth were you doing in Korea?

209
19:44.830 --> 19:46.790
They called you back ages ago--

210
19:46.873 --> 19:48.667
Long time no see.

211
19:49.501 --> 19:50.377
Sorry?

212
19:51.586 --> 19:53.338
When can I go see Mikogami?

213
19:54.631 --> 19:56.967
Sir, about that. I'm sorry, but--

214
19:57.050 --> 19:59.052
I don't want an apology.

215
19:59.553 --> 20:01.888
Just get me in to see him.

216
20:21.408 --> 20:22.492
What is it?

217
20:22.576 --> 20:24.244
What's up with the atmosphere?

218
20:24.786 --> 20:25.954
Well, sir,

219
20:26.747 --> 20:27.664
you see…

220
20:29.541 --> 20:32.127
Someone's waiting for you.

221
20:34.379 --> 20:36.965
INTERROGATION ROOM

222
20:41.636 --> 20:42.888
Hello!

223
20:43.513 --> 20:45.474
I'm from the Internal Affairs Division.

224
20:45.974 --> 20:47.142
Internal Affairs?

225
20:47.768 --> 20:50.479
I don't have any business with Internal Affairs.

226
20:51.188 --> 20:52.898
But you have business with Mikogami?

227
20:53.398 --> 20:54.649
Well,

228
20:55.275 --> 20:56.943
I'm sorry to disappoint,

229
20:57.027 --> 21:01.156
but Mikogami's execution was already carried out a few days ago.

230
21:01.239 --> 21:03.075
What's that supposed to mean?

231
21:04.409 --> 21:06.078
Did someone pull some strings?

232
21:09.289 --> 21:10.832
Please have a seat.

233
21:14.086 --> 21:15.587
Please sit down.

234
21:27.933 --> 21:29.768
Inspector Inose Hiroshi.

235
21:30.268 --> 21:33.605
You currently live alone in an apartment in Yokohama.

236
21:34.106 --> 21:39.778
And you're just barely managing to pay child support to your estranged wife.

237
21:40.737 --> 21:43.907
And you have a daughter who isn't even yours by blood?

238
21:46.284 --> 21:47.369
But

239
21:48.120 --> 21:49.913
even if you're not related by blood,

240
21:50.414 --> 21:51.498
I'd at least think

241
21:51.998 --> 21:56.545
you'd have some attachment to the kid you helped raise.

242
21:57.379 --> 22:00.715
Did you go to your daughter's kindergarten entrance ceremony?

243
22:01.299 --> 22:05.262
Any normal dad would have gone.

244
22:08.515 --> 22:11.643
What would you know? Do you have kids?

245
22:11.726 --> 22:14.187
From what I can tell, you're not even married yet.

246
22:17.399 --> 22:18.775
What you just said…

247
22:20.902 --> 22:22.404
I could make a stink about it.

248
22:23.155 --> 22:25.240
You're from the great Internal Affairs, so you'll know.

249
22:26.992 --> 22:29.578
Both my wife and daughter are sick of me.

250
22:29.661 --> 22:31.621
They won't give me a second thought.

251
22:31.705 --> 22:34.499
So can you just hurry up and get on with the inspection?

252
22:35.333 --> 22:36.460
Is that so?

253
22:39.337 --> 22:41.673
It's a little strange, isn't it?

254
22:42.799 --> 22:47.179
An inspection right when Emi's case is due for a follow-up investigation.

255
22:47.888 --> 22:49.681
What exactly is the issue here?

256
22:52.225 --> 22:54.019
KOREAN TRADITIONAL MARKET

257
22:54.102 --> 22:56.771
Thank you for taking the time to see me, Professor.

258
22:56.855 --> 22:58.023
Not at all.

259
22:58.523 --> 23:00.859
I had my own questions after our last conversation,

260
23:00.942 --> 23:02.861
so I was doing some more research anyway.

261
23:13.246 --> 23:15.373
Where did we leave off last time?

262
23:15.457 --> 23:18.084
You mentioned Emiri's descendants

263
23:18.168 --> 23:22.172
and some Japanese people who worshipped Emiri as a god.

264
23:30.013 --> 23:34.100
I was a little hesitant to mention it because it can be a touchy subject,

265
23:34.809 --> 23:39.147
but Japan has had such a huge impact on us.

266
23:40.607 --> 23:44.694
You must know about the numerous acts of torture and slaughter they committed

267
23:44.778 --> 23:46.696
during their occupation of Korea.

268
23:46.780 --> 23:49.699
What if I told you that's also related to the case?

269
23:50.200 --> 23:51.201
Okay.

270
23:56.039 --> 23:57.499
Then do you mean…

271
23:57.999 --> 23:58.959
Yes.

272
23:59.042 --> 24:02.546
There are records that some members of the Japanese forces stationed in Korea

273
24:02.629 --> 24:03.964
and the Kwantung Army

274
24:04.047 --> 24:06.925
would twist the joints of a person's limbs

275
24:07.008 --> 24:09.886
to torture their captives or intimidate enemies.

276
24:09.970 --> 24:11.721
The name of the unit was Tora.

277
24:12.847 --> 24:14.933
Meaning the Tiger Unit.

278
24:15.433 --> 24:18.603
And it is also said that in order to prolong the torture,

279
24:19.771 --> 24:21.898
they used opium.

280
24:22.482 --> 24:25.777
Just like Emiri's poppies.

281
24:27.362 --> 24:28.947
Then those people…

282
24:29.030 --> 24:29.948
That's right.

283
24:31.032 --> 24:34.119
There's a theory that the unit worshipped Emiri as their god.

284
24:36.830 --> 24:39.583
I went to great lengths to track down records on them.

285
24:39.666 --> 24:42.752
I brought copies of them for you.

286
24:43.962 --> 24:45.338
Let's see now.

287
24:45.922 --> 24:47.340
"Founding principles."

288
24:48.425 --> 24:51.928
"One fear breeds infinite fear,

289
24:53.054 --> 24:55.557
and all methods shall be concealed."

290
25:01.146 --> 25:02.314
One more thing.

291
25:02.981 --> 25:03.898
Do you remember

292
25:04.399 --> 25:08.236
the subordinate who naturalized to Korea with Emiri during the Imjin War,

293
25:08.320 --> 25:09.654
only to betray him?

294
25:09.738 --> 25:13.116
Yes, I remember you saying that there was a spy from the Japanese army.

295
25:13.867 --> 25:15.869
I found historical evidence

296
25:17.621 --> 25:20.790
that the spy's surname was Minamoto.

297
25:20.874 --> 25:22.250
Minamoto?

298
25:23.001 --> 25:26.338
Yes, the Minamoto of Minamoto Pharmaceuticals.

299
25:26.921 --> 25:29.883
And here, the commander's name

300
25:30.550 --> 25:32.677
is Minamoto Heihachi.

301
25:38.224 --> 25:39.934
It looks like this lineage

302
25:40.435 --> 25:45.315
are the ancestors of Emi Shunsuke, or rather, Minamoto Shunsuke.

303
25:49.027 --> 25:52.030
I have a picture of Minamoto Heihachi.

304
25:54.741 --> 25:55.950
This person here.

305
26:01.247 --> 26:06.378
At the time, Minamoto Heihachi did not return to Japan even after the defeat,

306
26:06.461 --> 26:08.296
but chose to stay in Korea.

307
26:08.880 --> 26:10.799
He became a Korean.

308
26:13.385 --> 26:15.136
Thank you for your help as always.

309
26:16.554 --> 26:18.098
Let's talk again.

310
26:27.816 --> 26:29.150
Minamoto, huh?

311
26:43.832 --> 26:44.999
You can come out now.

312
26:53.717 --> 26:55.135
I thought it might be you.

313
26:56.344 --> 26:58.513
You've been following me all this time?

314
26:59.889 --> 27:01.099
You're coming with me.

315
27:04.894 --> 27:08.064
Don't tell me what to do. Tell Seo Hyun-tae to come in person.

316
27:08.857 --> 27:09.691
You bastard.

317
27:12.652 --> 27:13.528
Easy.

318
27:15.405 --> 27:16.865
You're really asking for it.

319
27:29.669 --> 27:31.087
So you're a knife guy?

320
27:32.505 --> 27:33.548
Hold on.

321
27:33.631 --> 27:36.217
You're way out of line, you little shit.

322
27:41.973 --> 27:43.057
Go ahead.

323
27:50.690 --> 27:53.568
Still wet behind the ears, practically asking for it.

324
27:53.651 --> 27:55.737
You've got some nerve, you arrogant prick.

325
28:07.665 --> 28:10.335
Well? Have you come to your senses?

326
28:13.755 --> 28:16.007
What's the real reason you guys are in Korea?

327
28:18.510 --> 28:19.969
And what's this about Minamoto?

328
28:25.892 --> 28:27.018
Idiot.

329
28:34.150 --> 28:35.819
What is this uneasy feeling?

330
28:36.444 --> 28:39.781
Don't tell me the higher-ups way above us

331
28:39.864 --> 28:42.909
knew that it was Emi's doing all along?

332
28:43.910 --> 28:46.704
Maybe they really are all in bed with Minamoto--

333
28:46.788 --> 28:48.832
That case has nothing to do with this.

334
28:53.086 --> 28:54.546
Inspector Inose.

335
28:55.046 --> 28:58.633
We've received multiple reports regarding your neglect of duty,

336
28:58.716 --> 29:02.303
embezzlement of expenses, and abuse of authority.

337
29:02.387 --> 29:03.680
What the hell is it?

338
29:04.347 --> 29:07.308
What are you hiding, making such a fuss to stop me from digging?

339
29:07.392 --> 29:09.894
Is it Ito? Or is it Minamoto Pharmaceuticals?

340
29:12.772 --> 29:13.982
That's not the point.

341
29:14.065 --> 29:16.359
The point is Cindy! And Aki!

342
29:16.442 --> 29:18.778
Yoo I-jin and Lee Hyeon-seo.

343
29:21.531 --> 29:25.743
Do you know how many victims there've been because you all chose to turn a blind eye?

344
29:27.203 --> 29:28.454
Oh my.

345
29:29.038 --> 29:31.499
I didn't realize you were so emotional.

346
29:38.256 --> 29:41.593
Why do you insist on complicating things?

347
29:42.302 --> 29:45.430
It's a very simple matter.

348
29:51.644 --> 29:52.979
Please take a seat.

349
30:00.904 --> 30:02.530
Inspector Inose.

350
30:03.865 --> 30:07.327
You want to stay Rumi's father, do you not?

351
30:08.453 --> 30:09.412
In that case,

352
30:10.163 --> 30:14.042
you'd want to avoid being let go from the force like this, no?

353
30:14.626 --> 30:16.419
Well, that's one hell of a threat.

354
30:16.502 --> 30:20.548
You should put your family first, not your curiosity as a detective.

355
30:23.635 --> 30:25.887
But here's the thing.

356
30:28.348 --> 30:30.141
You don't smell like anything.

357
30:36.314 --> 30:38.858
Your Japanese is a little off too.

358
30:40.109 --> 30:41.986
What are you doing?

359
30:43.571 --> 30:45.615
I'm saying,

360
30:46.699 --> 30:48.284
you don't smell like a cop at all.

361
30:51.371 --> 30:52.747
Seo Hyun-tae.

362
30:55.833 --> 30:56.876
Bingo.

363
30:57.919 --> 30:59.629
Who are you?

364
31:07.136 --> 31:09.514
Japanese really isn't easy.

365
31:25.029 --> 31:26.406
Let me introduce myself again.

366
31:27.115 --> 31:29.742
I'm Yoon Soo-kyung. Korean National Intelligence Service.

367
31:36.124 --> 31:37.458
Did you not understand me?

368
31:38.960 --> 31:42.547
The Korean security service is working with the Japanese Public Security.

369
31:42.630 --> 31:45.174
Just think of it that way.

370
31:46.259 --> 31:47.093
Having fun?

371
31:53.099 --> 31:54.976
I'll get straight to the point.

372
31:55.977 --> 31:57.979
Take your hands off this matter.

373
32:21.878 --> 32:23.463
You're awake?

374
32:33.973 --> 32:35.224
Where am I?

375
32:36.225 --> 32:37.351
A print shop.

376
32:38.644 --> 32:40.688
Though it shut down a long time ago.

377
32:40.772 --> 32:42.190
No one comes here.

378
32:42.690 --> 32:44.358
No one would know if you died here.

379
32:45.026 --> 32:48.529
Given the lengths you guys are going, I guess my hunch was right.

380
32:49.447 --> 32:52.241
Yakuza? Who are you people, really?

381
32:52.909 --> 32:54.744
I warned you.

382
32:57.246 --> 32:59.165
Now, worry about staying alive.

383
33:15.306 --> 33:16.682
I hear you've been…

384
33:20.019 --> 33:21.312
so keen to meet me.

385
33:35.034 --> 33:36.285
Satisfied?

386
33:36.994 --> 33:38.663
You're Seo Hyun-tae?

387
33:46.796 --> 33:49.674
You see, Kim, I'm going to report you as a drug offender.

388
33:51.717 --> 33:53.678
Prison's better than dying, right?

389
33:59.600 --> 34:00.518
Hey!

390
34:15.324 --> 34:16.450
Come on, Kim.

391
34:23.624 --> 34:26.669
Are you actually curious how Hong Du-yeong died, or…

392
34:29.297 --> 34:31.174
are you curious why he died?

393
34:40.516 --> 34:43.311
Just stay put, as you are now.

394
34:56.449 --> 34:59.243
Seo Hyun-tae.

395
35:00.661 --> 35:02.788
Hey, don't overdo it.

396
35:04.457 --> 35:05.875
Seo Hyun-tae!

397
35:08.419 --> 35:09.879
Seo Hyun-tae, get back here.

398
35:19.430 --> 35:20.556
Are you okay?

399
35:22.475 --> 35:23.768
Hey, lackey.

400
35:27.063 --> 35:28.814
Go bring Seo Hyun-tae.

401
35:33.069 --> 35:34.695
I said bring Seo Hyun-tae.

402
35:54.298 --> 35:56.842
Don't get cocky, you piece of shit!

403
35:57.468 --> 35:58.928
Easy now.

404
36:00.012 --> 36:02.098
We should savor the fun.

405
36:02.932 --> 36:04.058
Move aside.

406
37:22.303 --> 37:24.430
Fine, you motherfuckers!

407
38:02.218 --> 38:03.844
What the hell are you all doing?

408
38:36.460 --> 38:37.545
Get him!

409
38:38.295 --> 38:39.839
Open the damn door!

410
38:52.184 --> 38:53.436
After him!

411
39:21.130 --> 39:23.466
Inose…

412
39:44.236 --> 39:46.238
We're not done talking yet.

413
39:52.912 --> 39:55.456
KIM SEOK

414
39:58.417 --> 40:01.712
Korean security service or not, keep me any longer and it's detention.

415
40:02.421 --> 40:03.714
Next time, bring a warrant.

416
40:08.677 --> 40:10.012
Inose.

417
40:21.774 --> 40:22.608
Kim Seok?

418
40:22.691 --> 40:25.444
The phone you have called is turned off…

419
40:28.447 --> 40:31.575
The phone you have called is turned off. Please leave a message…

420
40:33.744 --> 40:36.539
Damn it! Why aren't you picking up? Why?

421
40:42.628 --> 40:43.837
Shit!

422
40:45.214 --> 40:46.966
What the hell is going on?

423
40:49.593 --> 40:50.678
Why?!

424
45:13.023 --> 45:17.486
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
